   "subject": "Re: [unmarked] error message in running an occupancy model without site-level or observation-level covariates",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>hi Paul,</div><div><br></div><div> because all sites are observed to be occupied, the likelihood is maximized on the boundary (p, psi = 1) which is the reason for the warning. This is a valid solution (i.e., the MLEs are valid).</div><div><br></div><div>regards</div><div>andy</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
